@page "/pricing"
@attribute [MarketingPage]
@layout MarketingLayout
@using Relio.Application.Billing
@using Relio.Web.Components.Billing
@inject IBillingProvider BillingProvider

@* Plans are shown only when this instance has a billing provider (Billing:Provider=Stripe); the
   prices come from PlanCatalog, the same values the plan page and the limit use. Without billing the
   page says plainly that there are no paid plans. Static marketing: no owned data is read here. *@

<SeoHeadContent Title="@(BillingProvider.IsEnabled ? "Pricing" : "Hosting and pricing")"
                Description="@(BillingProvider.IsEnabled
                    ? $"Relio is free for up to {PlanCatalog.FreeActivePeopleLimit} active people. Relio Pro is {PlanCatalog.MonthlyPriceText}, or {PlanCatalog.YearlyPriceText}. Or run your own instance for free."
                    : "Choose this Relio instance or run your own. Learn about self-hosting requirements and optional mail delivery.")"
                CanonicalPath="/pricing" />

<header>
    <p class="rl-marketing-eyebrow">@(BillingProvider.IsEnabled ? "Simple pricing" : "Choose where Relio runs")</p>
    <h1>@(BillingProvider.IsEnabled ? "Plans and pricing" : "Hosting choices")</h1>
    <p class="rl-marketing-lead">
        @if (BillingProvider.IsEnabled)
        {
            <text>Start free. Subscribe when your notebook outgrows @PlanCatalog.FreeActivePeopleLimit active people.</text>
        }
        else
        {
            <text>Use an existing instance, or take responsibility for your own notebook's home.</text>
        }
    </p>
</header>

@if (BillingProvider.IsEnabled)
{
    <section class="rl-marketing-section" aria-labelledby="plans-heading">
        <h2 id="plans-heading">Plans on this instance</h2>
        <div class="rl-marketing-grid">
            <article class="rl-marketing-plan" aria-labelledby="plan-free-heading" data-testid="pricing-plan-free">
                <h3 id="plan-free-heading">@PlanCatalog.Free.DisplayName</h3>
                <p class="rl-marketing-price"><strong>$0</strong></p>
                <ul>
                    @foreach (var capability in PlanCatalog.Free.Capabilities)
                    {
                        <li>@capability</li>
                    }
                </ul>
                <MarketingStartLink />
            </article>
            <article class="rl-marketing-plan" aria-labelledby="plan-pro-heading" data-testid="pricing-plan-pro">
                <h3 id="plan-pro-heading">@PlanCatalog.Pro.DisplayName</h3>
                <p class="rl-marketing-price">
                    <strong>@PlanCatalog.YearlyMonthlyEquivalentText</strong> billed yearly (@PlanCatalog.YearlyPriceText),
                    or @PlanCatalog.MonthlyPriceText billed monthly
                </p>
                <ul>
                    @foreach (var capability in PlanCatalog.Pro.Capabilities)
                    {
                        <li>@capability</li>
                    }
                </ul>
                <div class="rl-marketing-actions">
                    @* The plan page needs a signed-in user: the sign-in redirect brings a visitor back to it. *@
                    <a class="rl-marketing-primary" href="@PlanText.PlanPagePath" data-enhance-nav="false"
                       data-testid="pricing-subscribe">Subscribe to Relio Pro</a>
                </div>
            </article>
        </div>
        <p>Prices are in US dollars. Archived people don't count towards the Free plan's limit, and
            nothing is deleted if you cancel: you keep everything you recorded and can still export it.
            Payments are handled by Stripe; Relio sends it your account email and an opaque account id
            only, never anything you have written about people.</p>
        <RelioPolicyLinks AriaLabel="Available policies for this instance" />
    </section>
}
else
{
    <section class="rl-marketing-section" aria-labelledby="instance-heading">
        <h2 id="instance-heading">Use this instance</h2>
        <p>You are viewing an instance of Relio. Its operator decides who can register and is responsible
            for hosting, mail delivery, backups and any published policies. Sign in if you already have an
            account, or create one when registration is available.</p>
        <MarketingStartLink ShowSignIn="true" />
        <p>This instance has no paid plans: every feature is included for every account.</p>
        <RelioPolicyLinks AriaLabel="Available policies for this instance" />
    </section>
}

<section id="self-hosting" class="rl-marketing-section" aria-labelledby="self-hosting-heading">
    <h2 id="self-hosting-heading">Run your own instance</h2>
    <p>Relio's source is available under the AGPL. A self-hosted instance runs without a billing
        provider or hosted product metrics, with no plans and no limits: billing is off unless an
        operator configures Stripe.</p>
    <p>You will need .NET 10, SQL Server, HTTPS, and durable externally stored Data Protection keys
        protected by a certificate or the supported Windows protection mode.
        Keep the database, keys and required decryption material backed up together.</p>
    <p>Apply migrations before a production upgrade. Configure SMTP only if you want confirmation,
        password-reset and reminder emails. Without it, the dashboard still works, but
        email-based password recovery is unavailable.</p>
    <p>Follow the <a href="https://github.com/kasuken/Relio/blob/main/docs/self-hosting.md">self-hosting deployment guide</a>,
        the <a href="https://github.com/kasuken/Relio/blob/main/README.md#getting-started">setup instructions</a>
        and <a href="https://github.com/kasuken/Relio/blob/main/docs/security/data-protection.md">protected-key guidance</a>
        before running an instance. <a href="https://github.com/kasuken/Relio/blob/main/LICENSE">Read the AGPL license</a>
        for your source-availability obligations.</p>
</section>

<section class="rl-marketing-section rl-marketing-faq" aria-labelledby="hosting-faq-heading">
    <h2 id="hosting-faq-heading">@(BillingProvider.IsEnabled ? "Pricing and hosting questions" : "Hosting questions")</h2>
    @if (BillingProvider.IsEnabled)
    {
        <details><summary>What counts towards the Free plan's limit?</summary><p>People who are not archived.
            Archive someone you are not keeping up with and they stop counting; restoring them counts again.
            Interactions, notes, reminders and difficult moments are not limited.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What happens if I cancel Relio Pro?</summary><p>Your subscription runs to the end of
            the period you paid for, then the account returns to the Free plan. Nothing is deleted: if you
            have more than @PlanCatalog.FreeActivePeopleLimit active people you keep them all, and you can't add
            or restore more until you archive some or subscribe again.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How do I change or cancel my subscription?</summary><p>Open Settings, then Plan and
            billing, and choose Manage billing. Stripe's billing portal lets you update your payment method,
            download invoices and cancel.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What if a payment fails?</summary><p>Relio Pro continues while Stripe retries the
            payment, and the plan page tells you what to update. If every retry fails, the account returns to
            the Free plan; nothing is deleted.</p></details>
    }
    <details><summary>Can I use Relio without hosted services?</summary><p>Yes. The relationship workspace
        does not need billing or analytics. Optional hosted product metrics are off by default,
        and there are no browser tracking scripts.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Who can create an account?</summary><p>The operator chooses Open, InviteOnly or Closed
        registration. A fresh instance always allows its first account so it can get an administrator.
        Invitation-only instances need an invitation link after that first account.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Is mail delivery required?</summary><p>No. With Email:Provider=None, the app sends no
        email. Configure SMTP to enable account confirmation, password-reset links and optional reminder
        emails, then review the instance's delivery and privacy responsibilities.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can I move my notebook later?</summary><p>Export full JSON from Settings and restore it
        into a fresh account. Contact-only vCard export is also available. Neither export contains your
        password or authentication secrets. Backups and their retention remain the operator's responsibility.</p></details>
</section>
